@startuml Keycloak_Authentication_Flow
title Keycloak Custom - Authentication Flow with No-Op Authenticator

participant User as U
participant "OIDC Endpoint" as EP
participant "Auth Flow Executor" as AFE
participant "NoOperationAuthenticator" as NOA
participant "Session Manager" as SM
participant "Token Generator" as TG
participant "Protocol Mapper" as PM
participant "Database" as DB

U -> EP: POST /auth/realms/master/protocol/openid-connect/auth\n?client_id=app&response_type=code
EP -> AFE: Initiate authentication flow
AFE -> NOA: Execute authenticator
NOA -> SM: Validate session/user
SM -> DB: Check user exists
DB --> SM: User found/verified
SM --> NOA: Session valid
NOA -> AFE: Complete authentication (no-op)
AFE -> TG: Generate tokens
TG -> PM: Apply protocol mappers
PM -> PM: Inject custom claims\n(NoOperationProtocolMapper)
PM --> TG: Claims injected
TG -> TG: Sign token (private key)
TG --> EP: Return token
EP --> U: Redirect with code/token

note over NOA
  No credential validation
  Demonstrates SPI pattern
  For testing/development only
end note

note over PM
  Injects claims into:
  - ID Token
  - Access Token
  - UserInfo response
end note

@enduml

@startuml Keycloak_Protocol_Mapper_Flow
title Keycloak Custom - Protocol Mapper Token Transformation

participant "Token\nGenerator" as TG
participant "OIDC Token\nMapper" as OTM
participant "NoOp Mapper\nChain" as NOM
participant "Claim\nExtractor" as CX
participant "Token\nSigner" as TS
participant "Client\nApplication" as CA

TG -> OTM: Start mapper pipeline
OTM -> NOM: Execute custom mapper
NOM -> NOM: Read mapper config
NOM -> CX: Extract claims from user
CX -> CX: Gather user attributes\nroles, groups, custom
CX --> NOM: Return claims
NOM -> NOM: Process claims\n(filter/transform)
NOM -> OTM: Return modified claims
OTM -> OTM: Apply default mappers
OTM -> TS: Token with all claims
TS -> TS: Sign with private key
TS --> CA: Send signed JWT
CA -> CA: Validate signature\nVerify claims\nAccess protected resources

note over NOM
  Custom mapper can:
  - Add claims
  - Remove claims
  - Transform values
  - Conditional logic
end note

@enduml

@startuml Keycloak_Deployment_Topology
